1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-1","kind":"phase-index","route":"/roadmap/phase-1","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-1","sourceHash":"be65e59cf30875406a9fcb336b8d274f2b496aad4f9cb017098517d1ad8c29c4","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:36.648Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Foundations","zh":"基础"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Learning a language doesn't happen overnight. It takes a while, so it's important to build a solid foundation of skills, tools, habits, and knowledge that will prepare you for the journey.","zh":"学习一门语言不会一蹴而就。这个过程需要时间，因此，建立扎实的技能、工具、习惯和知识基础非常重要，这些都会为接下来的学习之旅做好准备。"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"By the end of Phase 1, you won't be totally lost when looking at your target language. You'll have an environment and routine that push you toward success.","zh":"完成第 1 阶段后，面对目标语言时，你不会再完全不知所措。你将拥有一个能推动你走向成功的学习环境和日常安排。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This phase can seem a bit boring or slow at times, but setting up a strong base allows you to feel sure of your process and make continuous progress in all the other phases. If you already have some experience with your target language but are just starting with the Refold Method, you may move through this phase more quickly than expected.","zh":"这个阶段有时可能显得有些枯燥或进展缓慢，但打好基础能让你对自己的学习过程更有把握，并在其他所有阶段持续进步。如果你已经有一些目标语言经验，只是刚开始使用 Refold 方法，那么你可能会比预期更快地完成这个阶段。"}},{"id":"hour-estimates","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Hour Estimates","zh":"时间估算"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"table","rows":[[{"en":"Cousin","zh":"近似","header":true},{"en":"Similar","zh":"相近","header":true},{"en":"Neutral","zh":"中等","header":true},{"en":"Distant","zh":"遥远","header":true}],[{"en":"40","zh":"40","header":false},{"en":"75","zh":"75","header":false},{"en":"100","zh":"100","header":false},{"en":"150","zh":"150","header":false}]]},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"These are rough estimates to set expectations. Your actual time will depend on many factors. If you're somewhere in the ballpark, you're doing fine. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/categories-of-language-difficulty\">Categories of Language Difficulty</a>","zh":"这些只是用于建立预期的大致估算。你的实际用时会受到许多因素影响。只要大致在这个范围内，就说明你做得不错。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/categories-of-language-difficulty\">语言难度分类</a>"}},{"id":"sub-phases","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Sub-phases","zh":"子阶段"}},{"id":"1a-the-absolute-basics","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"1A — The Absolute Basics","zh":"1A — 绝对基础"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The very first thing you do is get your bearings. You'll learn your first 100 words, get familiar with the sounds of the language, and start noticing patterns in real content. Think of it as gearing up for the journey ahead.","zh":"你要做的第一件事是了解基本情况。你将学习最初的 100 个单词，熟悉这门语言的发音，并开始在真实内容中注意到其中的规律。可以把它看作是为接下来的学习之旅做好准备。"}},{"id":"1b-effort-tracking","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"1B — Effort Tracking","zh":"1B — 记录投入"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Tracking what you do and how much time you spend is directly correlated with success. This sub-phase is about setting up that system and building a consistent daily routine.","zh":"记录你做了什么以及花了多少时间，与成功直接相关。这个子阶段的重点是建立记录系统，并培养稳定的日常学习习惯。"}},{"id":"1c-begin-comprehension","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"1C — Begin Comprehension","zh":"1C — 开始理解"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The most common 1000 words make up about 70% of any language. You'll start learning those words and practicing real comprehension with native content, using tools and techniques to understand more than you otherwise could.","zh":"最常见的 1000 个单词约占任何语言的 70%。你将开始学习这些词，并通过母语者内容练习真正的理解能力，同时使用工具和技巧，让自己比原本能够理解更多内容。"}},{"id":"1d-get-comfortable","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"1D — Get Comfortable","zh":"1D — 适应学习节奏"}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Before taking the next leap, you need to settle into your routine and build comfort. You'll increase your daily time, introduce a new style of immersion, and solidify everything from the previous sub-phases.","zh":"在下一次跃进之前，你需要适应自己的学习安排并建立舒适感。你将增加每天的学习时间，引入一种新的沉浸方式，并巩固前几个子阶段学到的全部内容。"}}],"cards":[{"href":"/roadmap/phase-1/1a-the-absolute-basics","title":{"en":"1AThe Absolute Basics","zh":"1A绝对基础"}},{"href":"/roadmap/phase-1/1b-effort-tracking","title":{"en":"1BEffort Tracking","zh":"1B跟踪学习投入"}},{"href":"/roadmap/phase-1/1c-begin-comprehension","title":{"en":"1CBegin Comprehension","zh":"1C开始培养理解能力"}},{"href":"/roadmap/phase-1/1d-get-comfortable","title":{"en":"1DGet Comfortable","zh":"1D逐渐适应"}}]}}]
